   $q$Point $P$ lies on the perpendicular bisector of segment $AB$. $PA = 3x - 4$ and $PB = x + 10$. What is $PA$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$34$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-both-distances"},{"text":"$5$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-the-constant-instead-of-adding"},{"text":"$7$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gave-x-instead-of-the-length"},{"text":"$17$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$17$$q$, $q$Points on the perpendicular bisector are equidistant from $A$ and $B$, so $3x - 4 = x + 10$. Then $2x = 14$, $x = 7$, and $PA = 3(7) - 4 = 17$. The value $7$ is $x$, not the length.$q$, 'draft', null)
